1
00:00:01,921 --> 00:00:03,298
Hoo, hoo!

2
00:00:03,407 --> 00:00:04,334
Hi!

3
00:00:04,384 --> 00:00:06,412
It's me, Popcorn!

4
00:00:06,534 --> 00:00:11,764
Welcome to Popcorn Tales, the
cozy nest of bedtime stories.

5
00:00:12,076 --> 00:00:15,532
Hug your teddy, because
tonight's story is:

6
00:00:15,582 --> 00:00:18,847
Hansel, Gretel and the Cookie House!

7
00:00:23,460 --> 00:00:28,701
Once upon a time, in a wooden cottage
at the edge of a very big forest,

8
00:00:28,751 --> 00:00:33,360
there lived a woodcutter with his
two children, Hansel and Gretel.

9
00:00:33,999 --> 00:00:38,004
That long winter, the family
pantry was almost empty,

10
00:00:38,054 --> 00:00:42,413
and only one round loaf of bread
was left on the kitchen table.

11
00:00:43,010 --> 00:00:46,511
Tomorrow I will cut wood deep in the
forest, to trade it in the village for

12
00:00:46,561 --> 00:00:48,273
flour and a little milk,

13
00:00:48,323 --> 00:00:53,112
the father said, in a tired
voice, but full of hope.

14
00:00:53,765 --> 00:00:57,754
We will come with you, Father, and
we will help gather the dry branches,

15
00:00:57,804 --> 00:00:59,984
because together the work feels lighter,

16
00:01:00,034 --> 00:01:02,685
Hansel said, standing up straight.

17
00:01:03,245 --> 00:01:06,892
And I will bring my basket, to
pick blackberries along the way,

18
00:01:06,942 --> 00:01:08,735
if we find a bush full of them,

19
00:01:08,785 --> 00:01:11,893
Gretel said, with an excited smile.

20
00:01:12,510 --> 00:01:16,688
On the windowsill lived a brown
owl with a red bow on her head,

21
00:01:16,913 --> 00:01:20,257
who was listening to
everything very carefully.

22
00:01:20,866 --> 00:01:22,243
Hoo, hoo!

23
00:01:22,342 --> 00:01:25,951
The forest is big and full
of paths that look alike,

24
00:01:26,001 --> 00:01:29,081
so it is always good to
have a way back home,

25
00:01:29,131 --> 00:01:32,545
Popcorn said, blinking her round eyes.

26
00:01:33,188 --> 00:01:37,930
That night, Hansel tiptoed out to the
stream, and filled his pockets with

27
00:01:37,980 --> 00:01:42,741
white pebbles, which shone in
the moonlight like silver coins.

28
00:01:42,871 --> 00:01:46,752
Early in the morning, the three
of them walked into the forest,

29
00:01:46,802 --> 00:01:52,271
and at every bend in the path, Hansel
dropped a white pebble on the ground.

30
00:01:52,908 --> 00:01:57,024
The father started working in a
clearing, and the sound of the axe echoed

31
00:01:57,074 --> 00:01:59,558
slowly between the tall trunks.

32
00:02:02,931 --> 00:02:06,686
Gretel found a bush full of
dark, sweet blackberries,

33
00:02:06,736 --> 00:02:10,589
and the two children kept
picking, from bush to bush,

34
00:02:10,639 --> 00:02:13,386
farther and farther from the clearing.

35
00:02:14,027 --> 00:02:17,691
When they looked around,
the sun was already setting,

36
00:02:17,777 --> 00:02:21,677
and the sound of the axe had
faded away among the trees.

37
00:02:21,776 --> 00:02:25,134
Hansel, I do not know which
way the clearing is anymore,

38
00:02:25,184 --> 00:02:27,238
and the whole forest looks the same,

39
00:02:27,288 --> 00:02:30,966
Gretel said, holding her
brother's hand tightly.

40
00:02:31,616 --> 00:02:35,293
Stay calm, Gretel, because I
left a trail of white pebbles,

41
00:02:35,343 --> 00:02:38,107
and as soon as the moon
rises, we will see the way,

42
00:02:38,157 --> 00:02:40,863
Hansel said, in a steady voice.

43
00:02:41,517 --> 00:02:46,611
The moon rose round in the sky, and the
pebbles began to shine on the ground,

44
00:02:46,683 --> 00:02:50,875
one after another, like stars
that had fallen to the earth.

45
00:02:51,505 --> 00:02:54,905
The children followed the
silver trail all night long,

46
00:02:55,046 --> 00:02:59,516
step by step, until they saw the
light in the window of their home.

47
00:03:02,398 --> 00:03:05,659
Their father, who had been
searching for them with a lantern,

48
00:03:05,828 --> 00:03:11,562
ran to hug them both, and he had
never been so happy in all his life.

49
00:03:12,656 --> 00:03:16,509
A few days later, the father
had to go even farther,

50
00:03:16,559 --> 00:03:20,995
and the children went with him again,
but this time the stream was frozen and

51
00:03:21,045 --> 00:03:23,223
there were no pebbles to collect.

52
00:03:23,864 --> 00:03:28,625
So Hansel took the bread in his pocket,
and dropped crumbs along the path,

53
00:03:28,683 --> 00:03:30,931
one here and one there.

54
00:03:31,581 --> 00:03:36,906
The forest birds, who were also hungry
that winter, came flying down and ate

55
00:03:36,956 --> 00:03:38,897
the crumbs, one by one.

56
00:03:42,413 --> 00:03:46,946
When the children wanted to go back,
the bread trail had disappeared,

57
00:03:46,996 --> 00:03:50,424
and night was already
settling over the trees.

58
00:03:57,201 --> 00:04:01,649
The birds ate our path, but at least
they will not go to sleep hungry tonight,

59
00:04:01,699 --> 00:04:04,988
Gretel said, trying to
smile at her brother.

60
00:04:05,582 --> 00:04:06,958
Hoo, hoo!

61
00:04:07,045 --> 00:04:12,126
There is no use running in the dark,
because that only gets us more lost,

62
00:04:12,176 --> 00:04:16,107
so the best thing is to rest
together and wait for the sun,

63
00:04:16,157 --> 00:04:19,710
Popcorn said, landing on a low branch.

64
00:04:20,360 --> 00:04:24,177
The two children sat down on
the roots of an old oak tree,

65
00:04:24,304 --> 00:04:28,768
wrapped themselves in Gretel's shawl,
and watched the fireflies twinkling in

66
00:04:28,818 --> 00:04:30,018
the dark.

67
00:04:36,423 --> 00:04:39,522
As long as we are together,
I am not afraid of anything,

68
00:04:39,572 --> 00:04:42,886
Gretel, because you are the
bravest sister in the whole world,

69
00:04:42,936 --> 00:04:46,531
Hansel said, resting his
head on her shoulder.

70
00:04:47,142 --> 00:04:51,972
Popcorn stayed awake all night
long, with her eyes wide open,

71
00:04:52,114 --> 00:04:55,805
watching over them like a
gentle guardian of the forest.

72
00:04:59,132 --> 00:05:03,901
In the morning, a snow-white bird
landed on the branch of the oak tree and

73
00:05:03,951 --> 00:05:08,990
sang a melody so lovely that the
children got up to follow the sound.

74
00:05:12,464 --> 00:05:17,594
The bird flew from tree to tree, all
the way to a clearing full of flowers,

75
00:05:17,644 --> 00:05:22,044
and right in the middle stood the most
surprising house they had ever seen.

76
00:05:22,682 --> 00:05:27,021
The walls were made of golden cookies,
the roof was covered with white-iced

77
00:05:27,071 --> 00:05:32,193
cookies, and the windows were made
of clear sugar, sparkling in the sun.

78
00:05:32,770 --> 00:05:37,260
What a lovely smell of cinnamon and
honey, Hansel, my tummy is rumbling just

79
00:05:37,310 --> 00:05:38,475
from smelling it,

80
00:05:38,525 --> 00:05:41,995
Gretel said, with her eyes wide open.

81
00:05:42,685 --> 00:05:47,585
Hansel, who was very hungry, broke
off a piece of the roof's edge,

82
00:05:47,671 --> 00:05:50,918
and Gretel tasted a corner
of the sugar window.

83
00:05:53,157 --> 00:05:58,640
Then, from inside the house, came
a hoarse and very cross voice.

84
00:05:59,245 --> 00:06:01,331
Who is nibbling at my house?

85
00:06:01,772 --> 00:06:04,512
Who is eating my roof and my window?

86
00:06:04,711 --> 00:06:09,597
the old neighbour asked from
inside, in a very grumpy voice.

87
00:06:10,232 --> 00:06:14,557
The children looked at each other,
embarrassed, and Gretel took a deep breath

88
00:06:14,607 --> 00:06:17,174
before answering with the whole truth.

89
00:06:17,727 --> 00:06:21,743
It was us, ma'am, Hansel and
Gretel, and we are very sorry,

90
00:06:21,793 --> 00:06:25,088
because we are lost and we have
been hungry since yesterday,

91
00:06:25,138 --> 00:06:28,079
Gretel said, in a polite voice.

92
00:06:29,182 --> 00:06:33,173
The door opened with a long
creak, and there stood a short,

93
00:06:33,223 --> 00:06:39,201
round old woman, with white hair in a
bun, round glasses and an apron covered

94
00:06:39,251 --> 00:06:40,451
in flour.

95
00:06:43,600 --> 00:06:47,823
I spent the whole autumn baking
every single cookie of this house,

96
00:06:47,873 --> 00:06:51,878
and I never share my sweets
with anybody, not ever,

97
00:06:51,990 --> 00:06:55,835
the old neighbour grumbled,
gripping her wooden spoon.

98
00:06:56,522 --> 00:07:01,069
Hansel and Gretel lowered their heads
and offered to help fix the damage,

99
00:07:01,119 --> 00:07:05,088
because they thought it was fair to
work to pay for what they had eaten.

100
00:07:05,661 --> 00:07:09,506
I can sweep the whole house, and my
brother can carry the firewood and the

101
00:07:09,556 --> 00:07:10,869
water from the well,

102
00:07:10,919 --> 00:07:14,749
Gretel said, already picking
up the broom from the corner.

103
00:07:15,380 --> 00:07:18,455
The neighbour grumbled a
little more, but she agreed,

104
00:07:18,505 --> 00:07:23,816
and the children worked all day long,
sweeping, washing bowls and carrying

105
00:07:23,866 --> 00:07:25,169
wood for the oven.

106
00:07:28,087 --> 00:07:32,099
From the top of the shelf,
Popcorn noticed something curious:

107
00:07:32,149 --> 00:07:37,466
in that house there was no second plate,
no second cup and no second chair.

108
00:07:38,060 --> 00:07:39,437
Hoo, hoo!

109
00:07:39,515 --> 00:07:43,996
This lady is not wicked, I
think she is just very lonely,

110
00:07:44,046 --> 00:07:48,268
and she has forgotten how nice it
is to have visitors at the table,

111
00:07:48,318 --> 00:07:52,593
Popcorn said, in a low
voice, to the children.

112
00:07:53,240 --> 00:07:57,718
And it was true, because the village
children were afraid of her grumbling,

113
00:07:57,768 --> 00:08:01,662
and nobody had knocked on the
door of the cookie house for many,

114
00:08:01,712 --> 00:08:02,987
many years.

115
00:08:04,068 --> 00:08:07,866
Late in the afternoon, the
neighbour lit the big stone oven,

116
00:08:07,916 --> 00:08:11,760
because she wanted to bake a new
batch of cookies to mend the roof.

117
00:08:11,908 --> 00:08:17,090
Girl, look inside there and tell me if
the oven is hot enough for the cookies,

118
00:08:17,242 --> 00:08:20,933
the neighbour asked, pushing
her glasses up her nose.

119
00:08:21,557 --> 00:08:27,326
Gretel, who was clever and very calm,
thought the fire was far too strong,

120
00:08:27,376 --> 00:08:31,124
and she chose to stay close
to the old lady to help her.

121
00:08:31,679 --> 00:08:35,326
I have never used such a big oven,
could you show me how it is done,

122
00:08:35,376 --> 00:08:36,520
very carefully?

123
00:08:36,570 --> 00:08:39,818
Gretel asked, holding the wooden paddle.

124
00:08:40,438 --> 00:08:44,783
The neighbour leaned in to look inside
the oven, but her glasses slipped,

125
00:08:44,869 --> 00:08:49,291
she could not see the edge of the fire,
and the tip of her lilac shawl came

126
00:08:49,341 --> 00:08:50,963
close to the embers.

127
00:08:51,603 --> 00:08:56,872
At that very moment, Hansel and Gretel
grabbed the old lady by her apron and

128
00:08:56,922 --> 00:09:01,836
pulled her back, firmly and
kindly, away from the heat.

129
00:09:03,979 --> 00:09:08,748
The shawl did not even burn, nobody
was hurt, and the neighbour sat on the

130
00:09:08,798 --> 00:09:13,406
kitchen floor, looking at the two
children with tears in her eyes.

131
00:09:13,978 --> 00:09:19,350
You ate my window, and even so you took
care of me, as if I were part of your

132
00:09:19,400 --> 00:09:20,347
family,

133
00:09:20,397 --> 00:09:24,283
the neighbour said, her
voice trembling with feeling.

134
00:09:25,373 --> 00:09:29,476
That night, the neighbour took an
enormous tin full of cookies out of a

135
00:09:29,526 --> 00:09:33,593
cupboard, a tin she had
kept locked away for years.

136
00:09:34,237 --> 00:09:38,729
She set out three plates, three cups
of warm milk and three chairs at the

137
00:09:38,779 --> 00:09:43,590
table, and for the first time in a
very long while, the cookie house was

138
00:09:43,640 --> 00:09:45,123
filled with laughter.

139
00:09:45,707 --> 00:09:50,090
I used to think that if I shared
my sweets, they would run out,

140
00:09:50,140 --> 00:09:54,595
but today I found out that sharing
makes everything taste much better,

141
00:09:54,714 --> 00:09:58,350
the neighbour said, laughing
along with the children.

142
00:09:58,996 --> 00:10:02,696
In the morning, she filled
Gretel's basket with bread,

143
00:10:02,746 --> 00:10:06,682
cookies and a jar of honey,
and showed them the way back,

144
00:10:06,732 --> 00:10:09,841
which went past a wide and calm lake.

145
00:10:10,486 --> 00:10:14,136
At the edge of the lake, a
white duck swam up to them,

146
00:10:14,236 --> 00:10:17,886
and carried first Gretel
and then Hansel on its back,

147
00:10:17,944 --> 00:10:22,386
one at a time, because both of them
together would have been too heavy for it.

148
00:10:24,489 --> 00:10:25,866
Hoo, hoo!

149
00:10:25,971 --> 00:10:30,730
What a kind duck, and what a
wise idea to cross one at a time,

150
00:10:30,780 --> 00:10:34,305
Popcorn said, flying low over the water.

151
00:10:34,900 --> 00:10:39,522
On the other side of the lake, the
children soon recognized the trees,

152
00:10:39,608 --> 00:10:44,244
the frozen stream and the smoke
rising from their own chimney.

153
00:10:45,346 --> 00:10:48,769
The father was standing at
the door, watching the road,

154
00:10:48,819 --> 00:10:53,477
and when he saw his children coming
home, he ran with open arms to hug them

155
00:10:53,527 --> 00:10:55,566
both at the same time.

156
00:10:56,223 --> 00:11:00,332
They shared the bread, the cookies
and the honey with their father,

157
00:11:00,390 --> 00:11:04,693
and that day the wooden cottage had
the fullest table of the whole winter.

158
00:11:05,321 --> 00:11:10,049
Ever since then, every Sunday, the
neighbour opens the door of the cookie

159
00:11:10,099 --> 00:11:14,771
house to the village children, with
a tray full of sweets and a great big

160
00:11:14,821 --> 00:11:16,021
smile.

161
00:11:17,622 --> 00:11:22,059
And Hansel and Gretel learned that
brothers and sisters look after each other,

162
00:11:22,109 --> 00:11:25,286
and that a treat you share
always tastes sweeter.

163
00:11:25,920 --> 00:11:30,897
And at night, when the moon rises over
the forest, Popcorn sings in a low

164
00:11:30,947 --> 00:11:35,292
voice, and the two children sleep
peacefully in the wooden cottage,

165
00:11:35,378 --> 00:11:37,708
dreaming of cookie roofs.

166
00:11:47,353 --> 00:11:48,553
The End.

167
00:11:50,268 --> 00:11:50,980
Hoo...

168
00:11:51,030 --> 00:11:52,054
Psst!

169
00:11:52,104 --> 00:11:53,676
Are you still awake?

170
00:11:53,830 --> 00:11:55,884
Did you like tonight's story?

171
00:11:56,043 --> 00:12:01,397
Hansel, Gretel and Popcorn showed us
that brothers and sisters look after each

172
00:12:01,447 --> 00:12:05,446
other, that calm and clever
thinking help us find the way,

173
00:12:05,496 --> 00:12:08,448
and that everything is
sweeter when we share.

174
00:12:08,710 --> 00:12:13,016
Good night, sleep tight, and
have the sweetest dreams.

175
00:12:13,312 --> 00:12:18,210
Grown-ups: if you enjoyed it,
please subscribe to Popcorn Tales,

176
00:12:18,260 --> 00:12:20,665
for more stories at bedtime.

177
00:12:20,969 --> 00:12:22,169
Hoo...

